## 1. The proved analytic reduction (this is what makes a certificate, §7.2)

> Let S ⊆ V(G) with G[V∖S] bipartite and |S| = OCT(G). Color G[V∖S] properly with 2 colors; give each vertex of S a distinct fresh color. Edges inside V∖S are proper; every edge touching S has its S-endpoint in a fresh color unused by V∖S, and S's fresh colors are pairwise distinct. So **χ(G) ≤ 2 + OCT(G)**, i.e. **OCT(G) ≥ χ(G) − 2, for every finite G**. ∎

